---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Keiter & Co. Academy"
  description="A self-paced curriculum that teaches a new operator how to run a Keiter & Co. build from zero. Intake, three-document workflow, build, launch, and ongoing client care."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-warm-white border-b border-stone/20 section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-moss uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">Keiter &amp; Co. Academy</p>
        <h1 class="mb-6">
          Learn to run a Keiter &amp; Co. build from zero.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-bark/80 mb-8 max-w-xl">
          A self-paced curriculum for anyone Olivia and Alex trust to carry the methodology forward. Start with what AI is. Finish knowing how to run a complete client engagement, from intake to launch to ongoing care.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
          <a
            href="/curriculum"
            class="inline-flex items-center bg-rust text-cream font-semibold px-6 py-3 rounded hover:bg-bark transition-colors no-underline min-h-[44px]"
          >
            Start the curriculum
          </a>
          <a
            href="/start"
            class="inline-flex items-center border border-bark text-bark font-semibold px-6 py-3 rounded hover:bg-bark hover:text-cream transition-colors no-underline min-h-[44px]"
          >
            Not sure where to begin?
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Hero image placeholder -->
      <div class="mt-12 w-full aspect-video bg-mauve-faint rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center text-stone text-sm italic" aria-hidden="true">
        <!-- BUILDNOTES: Replace with real photo. Subject: wide shot of Olivia at her desk in the farmhouse. Soft natural light. Real and unposed. Work in progress on screen. Kids' artwork on the wall behind her. Aspect ratio 16:9. -->
        Photo placeholder: Olivia at her desk, farmhouse, natural light, 16:9
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who this is for -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="mb-10">Who this is for</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
        {[
          {
            heading: 'Future Keiter operators',
            body: 'Anyone Olivia or Alex brings on to run builds. The curriculum transfers the full methodology, nothing held back.',
          },
          {
            heading: 'Self-learners',
            body: 'Small business owners, solo builders, and anyone who wants a sober, practical operating system for building with AI.',
          },
          {
            heading: 'Other builders',
            body: 'People who build sites for clients and want to see how a real methodology, not a template, actually works.',
          },
        ].map((card) => (
          <div class="bg-warm-white border border-stone/30 rounded-lg p-6 hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-transform shadow-sm">
            <h3 class="text-lg mb-2">{card.heading}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-bark/80 max-w-none">{card.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Curriculum overview -->
  <section class="section bg-warm-white border-y border-stone/20">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="mb-3">The curriculum</h2>
      <p class="text-bark/80 mb-10">
        Six parts. Twenty-three modules. Real methodology, no shortcuts.
      </p>
      <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {[
          { part: 'Part 1', title: 'Welcome to Keiter & Co.', desc: 'Who we are, what we believe, the standing principles, and the partnership structure.', href: '/curriculum/welcome' },
          { part: 'Part 2', title: 'The tools', desc: 'What AI is, what Claude is, and when to reach for each Claude surface.', href: '/curriculum/tools' },
          { part: 'Part 3', title: 'How we think', desc: 'Voice, tone, the hard formatting rules, and how to hold the principles when it is hard.', href: '/curriculum/how-we-think' },
          { part: 'Part 4', title: 'How we build', desc: 'The three-document system, phased prompts, build standards, and the Definition of Done.', href: '/curriculum/how-we-build' },
          { part: 'Part 5', title: 'How we run the business', desc: 'Intake, proposals, infrastructure, launch, and ongoing client care.', href: '/curriculum/business' },
          { part: 'Part 6', title: 'Practice', desc: 'A real walkthrough, a capstone build, and the reference templates you will use every time.', href: '/curriculum/practice' },
        ].map((part) => (
          <a
            href={part.href}
            class="block bg-cream border border-stone/30 rounded-lg p-5 hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-moss transition-all no-underline group shadow-sm"
          >
            <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-moss uppercase tracking-wide block mb-1">{part.part}</span>
            <h3 class="text-base mb-2 group-hover:text-rust transition-colors">{part.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-bark/70 max-w-none">{part.desc}</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What success looks like -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="mb-4">What success looks like</h2>
      <p class="text-bark/80 mb-8">
        A learner who completes the curriculum can run a Keiter &amp; Co. engagement end to end.
      </p>
      <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 list-none p-0 m-0 max-w-2xl">
        {[
          'Explain what AI is, what Claude is, and choose the right Claude surface for a given task.',
          'Hold the five standing principles without prompting.',
          'Run a Keiter-format intake conversation and produce a brief.',
          'Write a decision log, a spec, and a multi-phase kickoff for a small client site.',
          'Operate a build session phase-by-phase, with handoff notes, against the full Definition of Done.',
          'Build to WCAG 2.2 AA, SEO, AEO, and the Keiter online personality standards.',
          'Hand off a finished site with a Welcome to the Family guide.',
          'Support a Care Plan client month over month.',
        ].map((item) => (
          <li class="flex gap-3 text-sm">
            <span class="text-moss font-bold mt-0.5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
            <span>{item}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
